# Unity 6.5 Architecture

- Engine: Unity 6.5 (6000.5.x), C#. This repo is not Unreal/Blueprint.
- Data-driven: ScriptableObjects / JSON importers. No hardcoded tunables in MonoBehaviours.
- Thin scenes; gameplay logic lives in domain systems under `Assets/Scripts/`.

## System folders (single responsibility)

- `Run/` — run state, character background, symptom severities
- `Level/` — card queue, decisions, stat deltas, hidden vars
- `Stats/` — four meters, thresholds, fail reasons
- `Split/` — four minigame modes via `ISplitMinigame`
- `Therapy/` — merge rules engine
- `Skills/` — DBT limited-use replacement choices
- `Progression/` — XP, level index, unlocks, modifiers
- `Presentation/` — UI only; no gameplay rules in widgets

## Performance and input

- Avoid per-frame allocations in card flow; pool UI cards when needed.
- Addressables optional later; MVP may use SO + Resources if documented.
- Input System: swipe/touch + mouse drag + keyboard arrows on PC.
- All player-facing strings via `BPD.Localization.Loc` keys (Unity Localization deferred until package supports EntityId on 6000.5).
- UI stack: uGUI + adaptive shell (`AdaptiveShell`, safe area, portrait/landscape). See `ui-adaptive.mdc`.
- Platforms: mobile + PC from day one — no desktop-only layouts.
- Actions: **1 column in portrait**; landscape max **2** when wide enough. Tap height ≥ 104. Typography floors in `ui-adaptive.mdc`.
- Input: Unity Input System (`com.unity.inputsystem` 1.18+ embedded/patched); Player activeInputHandler = Input System Only.
- Dynamic Batching disabled per platform in Player settings.
